Error accumulation means reporting independent failures together before continuing with output.
[Effect](/lore/effect-basics) 4's [`Effect.validate`](https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/blob/289a53f7b1fc40049219c6e69022db2fb859c356/packages/effect/src/Effect.ts#L612-L619) evaluates every collection element.
It returns all failures as a non-empty array when any element fails.
Successful values are discarded in that case.

## Worked example: collect snippet failures

The [code-snippets pipeline](/lore/code-snippets) applies this operation to Markdown code blocks.
Each job carries its parsed document node and source path.
`prepareCode` parses each request before rendering configured code.
A parse failure ends that job; validation continues across the other jobs.

The collection starts here:

```ts repo=rat-stack path=packages/code-snippets/src/pipeline.ts at=4cd7cbbdb90386426f44643f6fc5b8e6c6e4286a lines=303-312 title="Validate each fence job"

```

The `Effect.mapError` after `Effect.validate` turns collected failures into one `CodeBuildFailed` error.
It retains the individual failures and formats each one as a message with [diagnostic context](/lore/errors-are-part-of-the-interface).

```ts repo=rat-stack path=packages/code-snippets/src/pipeline.ts at=4cd7cbbdb90386426f44643f6fc5b8e6c6e4286a lines=359-369 title="Keep each failure in the build error"

```

The site generator follows this order:
1. Collect and verify code blocks.
2. Run `prepareCode` over the jobs.
3. Report diagnostics and construct the Code component from prepared snippets.

## Check the failure path

The P7 [property test](https://github.com/joelhooks/rat-stack/blob/4cd7cbbdb90386426f44643f6fc5b8e6c6e4286a/packages/code-snippets/test/pipeline.test.ts#L413-L441) generates one to eight jobs with unknown repository names.
It expects one message and one `CodeUnknownRepo` failure per job.
The test increments a counter only in a success continuation after `prepareCode`.
For these invalid jobs, the counter stays zero.

This proves the continuation does not run; it does not observe filesystem asset writes.

Read [property-based testing](/lore/property-based-testing) for generated inputs, and the [snippet pipeline](/lore/code-snippets) for the full build path.
